cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or data, please cite the following."
title: "Conserved Chemistry, Divergent Grammar: how antibodies read protein interfaces differently from co-evolved partners"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Raut
    given-names: Meetrayu
  - family-names: Sinharay
    given-names: Amrita
  - family-names: Kale
    given-names: Anup
    email: anup.kale@mitwpu.edu.in
repository-code: "https://github.com/rautmeetu1004-cmyk/antibody-antigen-recognition-grammar"
abstract: >-
  A matched-pipeline comparison of 512 antibody-antigen and 2,292 co-evolved protein-protein
  interfaces: shared chemistry at the chemical-class level, divergent residue-pair grammar
  localised to tyrosine-hydroxyl backbone readout. Includes the full analysis code, data
  manifests, result tables, figures, and tools (grammar scorer, epitope predictor).
keywords:
  - antibody-antigen recognition
  - protein-protein interfaces
  - structural bioinformatics
  - interface chemistry
  - epitope
  - paratope
